t members; PREDICTED under leg (b) is A3=0 and A1=1, both archive-confirmed at display precision; new-run checks remain mandatory above — a leg-(a)-passing disagreement on any OTHER row is a finding reported with operands, never an auto-miss. The 0.68/1.38 table values are predictions under leg (b). The P042 "A3 shadow pair" means exactly: A3-keyed record present, leg-(a) consistent, wouldGate self-consistent — plus the leg-(b) confirmation. Display rounds to two decimals (R/table figures display only; grading uses the P042 exact-rational interval). The exact A3-fail/A1-pass interval from the table operands is separation interval (99/146, 108/78] (displayed decimals 0.678082, 1.384615 are not exact endpoints) graded by the P042 exact-rational rule (no rounding, no band table); 1.0 sits interior (filed point-differences by exact subtraction: 144/42, 108/78, 297/171, 180/37, 54/23, 133/53, 99/146). Row-to-signal key: the seven TP_ELECT fire rows (of eleven TP_ELECT rows total) are the seven current actual-path signals (A1 and A3 fire-but-declined under his kill-all); the SIGNAL event count is reported separately under the comparison contract and is not the same invariant. A1 stop 1.16503 to 1.16508 is the 5-point stop move (display-derived, never _Point-derived; R ratios are unit-free and survive any digits setting) (R 1.48 to 1.38; the 1.16503 baseline is the post-gate SIDE1X liveStop on the filed A1 archive rows, agreeing v158 line 54 A1-BASE sl=1.16503); A3 live stop 1.16274 is the post-gate SIDE1X liveStop on the filed A3 archive rows (archive fact with entry 1.16213 and actual R 1.62). The A2 row is declined-and-evaluated — baseline fire means S5-evaluated in baseline with its ext1 read printed, vetoed before latch (no TP_ELECT row); current means silent, no signal/fire outcome — and exempt from shadow-R/table acceptance (its mandatory ext1 acceptance is pxExt1/slot/provenance at archive precision: equality after applying the archive's documented five-decimal formatter to the finite probe value; the three obligations stay separate — expected A2 price at archive precision, slot 13, origin stamp plus ordered provenance join; an origin-only join never validates the ext1 price; halt-state rows (sl41_halt != -) are an explicit join-halt class: stamp/site freshness grades, origin-price/origin-time legacy - fields never enter printed-precision equality); it remains subject to the universal actualGate/live-operand checks, serialization checks, and terminal/diagnostic contract — the exemption is shadow-R-only, never broader; the archive SIDE1E r1=7.30 for A2 (SLIMBR-carried value) is provenance context only, never a grading operand — a differing probe rExt1 at the A2 row is not a miss (and the post-gate archive SIDE1E row independently agrees: r1=7.30, ruleSlot=13). The A2 seed-bar instrument evaluation (STOPREF) is the seed-bar evaluation of the A2 bar, not a signal. A2's veto refusal is order-specific to this window (veto site precedes latch with the R-gate passing first here), never a general claim about evaluation order. Sentinel convention, table and probe (SLEXT481's legacy 17-field convention differs and is not amended here): -999 marks absent EXT1 integer IDs plus undefined ext1Imb under P036 — never prices, never ratios; s0/s1 slot/imb fields print post-cast selector ints verbatim (they are the cast values the L9662-L9663 predicates consumed — initial -1 reads -1: absent slot, unread imbalance, and genuine -1 are not distinguished — stated, not hidden; source-identity conclusions involving imbalance cannot prove the original flow value was integral; the P011 count convention defers to this note); every other N/A prints '-' (prices, text, datetimes, guard-blocked ratios - with the s0px/s1px carve-out inline here: no-candidate s0px/s1px print 0 paired with slot -1, never a sentinel and never '-'); 0 means computed zero. P036 enumerates the per-field override; where this paragraph and P036 differ on a named field, P036 governs