only — never provenance, never higher-precision source equality); five-fire identity is judged from those values, never five-decimal archive displays; (c) gate results actual-vs-shadow. Slot identity establishes source identity, never price difference; displayed price equality establishes neither provenance nor exact numeric equality. PREDICTED source-changed bars under this rule: 10:35 (A2 seed), 08-28 16:20 (A1), 09-08 16:40 (A3) per SHADOW sel rows — all three already declined. Five other fires PREDICTED identical because live stop already equals s1px there (prediction only, resolved by prints — never a pre-accepted result). Emergent reading named as prediction: where ext1 equals s1 the rule reduces to removing the s0 branch for defined-ext1 bars — the section 3 slot prints resolve it per row (s0px/s1px now saved so the liveSel=0 rows are decidable too). All ext1 differences in this run are counterfactual (print-only). extDistPts output is an integer-valued double via MathRound (the EA's existing primitive, cf. L5469), printed via DoubleToString(m,0) without decimals; the rounded double is range-tested against the filed |extDistPts| <= 99999 range before the offline (int) interpretation — out-of-range prints INVALID; sign fixed here: positive = protective-side displacement, zero = rounded at-entry, negative = non-protective-side displacement (never "magnitude" for a signed negative); `-0` is accepted and read as 0. ladOriginPx prints lossless per P036; the offline provenance join compares it as printed-precision: equality after applying the legacy row's documented price formatter (five-decimal DoubleToString) to the probe origin value, with datetime/site equality under their defined encodings — a printed-precision provenance check, never lossless-vs-rounded numeric identity. MANDATORY per-row origin-vs-live check: ladOriginPx == currentPrice as identical reconstructed IEEE-754 binary64 bit patterns after parsing canonical tokens, including signed zero (distinct symbols — global written at L8773 vs local at L8753, same iOpen(barShift-1) expression in the same call; any inequality falsifies the required origin/live consistency; halt with operands and diagnose on disk (separate series reads, failed reads, or source/mapping defects are other possible causes; equal prices do not independently establish freshness) or the globals are stale; is corroborating only on the same input series (a stale global can repeat the open; the ladOriginStamp == barTime equality is the staleness falsifier)). The entryPx==currentPrice textual check is FREE and proves nothing (one variable printed twice; schema/duplication invariant only; kept, never counted as a falsifier).

## 3. Probe form (print-only = no strategy-state mutation, no NEW live selector/gate substitution (the S1-LIVE-STOPFIX-001 rewire is already live in 6C2E4028), no change to existing strategy control flow, no unload request — terminal conditions latch probe silence only and the run always completes the range; THREE insertions A+B+C with outer-scope carries (A, B, and C ALL cleared as literal source text pasted in P032, except the two explicitly named STAGE-1-bound RHS expressions covered by the addendum hunk; the STAGE-1 exact-diff gate checks the build tree against that text plus the hunk); fields=38 payload + fixed envelope; section-1 rule NOT executed)

Insertion A (before the L9618 comment that annotates the selector block (identical scope, cleaner diff), in the straight-line S5 tail shared with C — automatic per-evaluation storage, never static candidate state): carry declarations `double probe_inSlRef = slRef; int probe_sel = 99; double probe_slLive = -1e308; int probe_s0slot = -2147483647; int probe_s0imb = -2147483647; int probe_s1slot = -2147483647; int probe_s1imb = -2147483647; double probe_s0px = -1e308; double probe_s1px = -1e308; bool probe_bSaved = false;` — ten initialized declarations (one live copy, one false witness, eight fixed poison values: -1e308 for doubles, -2147483647 for ints, 99 for the selector — none of them a plausible live value, so a skipped B still fails loudly (poison plus probe_bSaved are falsifiers for detectable omission or miswiring in B (source verification stays mandatory; a coherent-but-complete miswiring outside the P034 identities is not claimed detected); absent-candidate state after successful B is slot -1 with price 0.0 by design); detection lives in the witness plus the P034 crossed-assignment identities, never in uninitialized storage; kept as falsifiers only (exact B-assignment verification and complete S5 publication/dominance proof stay mandatory disk gates)). Scope proof (measured on disk 2026-09-18): A, the selector block, B, and C lie on the same enclosing straight-line tail — the loop census over L8779→L9670 finds six for/while openers (L9051, L9218, L9230, L9368, L9386, L9506), all closed before the L9532 straight-line tail, and exactly one loop between L9532 and C — the L9632 selector walk itself; inside the selector block, all break/continue statements target the L9632 loop and no return or other exit bypasses B — so every path from A to C passes B; A-site and C-site brace depth are identical with no conditional/switch boundary between them (STAGE-1 asserts the literal depth numbers for both the A site and the C site on the instrumented tree, else halt — a boundary would fail loudly at the 0/0 gate as a wasted build, never silently; A-to-B-to-C domination is unprovable from this page alone (the L8779-L9606 interval rides as a disk item - the STAGE-1 assertions are the sole text check, never page proof) (N-3)); automatics are fresh per EvaluateClosedBar call (sole invocation EvaluateClosedBar(1,currentBarTime) at OnTick L11214; STAGE-1 requires the EvaluateClosedBar invocation census, else halt), and no per-candidate loop exists to stale the carries; probe_bSaved therefore detects never-assigned, and staleness across evaluations is impossible by this construction (STAGE-1 re-verifies the census on the instrumented tree, else halt). Insertion B (post-L9665, pre-L9666, inside the selector block): assignments only — `probe_sel = s1x_sel; probe_slLive = slRef; probe_s0slot = s1x_s0slot; probe_s0imb = s1x_s0imb; probe_s1slot = s1x_s1slot; probe_s1imb = s1x_s1imb; probe_s0px = s1x_s0px; probe_s1px = s1x_s1px; probe_bSaved = true;` — eight carry saves plus the witness assignment (nine statements). Silent saves, no printing, no computation. Insertion C (post-L9670: first probe statement after the gate test, placed before the L9671 comment — slDist/tpDist/tpOk all exist as live-computed values): probe-owned storage `static uint probe_seq = 0; const uint PROBE_CAP = 20000; static bool probe_schema_done = false; static bool probe_capped = false; static bool probe_dead = false;` (emission latch, counter, cap flag, and shared terminal latch — not candidate state; static lifetime is the EA execution, fresh execution resets; counter updates as `probe_seq = probe_seq + 1`, never ++/--; `uint` is MQL5's unsigned 32-bit int — there is no `unsigned int` keyword; const uint PROBE_CAP is automatic const (re-initialized per call), so the four counted statics are probe_seq/probe_schema_done/probe_capped/probe_dead); `string probe_keys[38]; string probe_vals[38]; string probe_line; string probe_tmpA; string probe_tokPx;` (one single-definition-site ordered 38-key array plus one per-record 38-value array plus line, ONE datetime temp probe_tmpA (used five times across record types: three common NORMAL-path encode-stores per step 5b plus the defined-only ext1BarTime store plus the BSAVE_FAIL barTime encode (a fallback NORMAL row uses the temp three times); the two-temp wording and the both-referenced gate are dropped with probe_tmpB; the single temp cannot trip the 0/0 unused-variable gate by construction (stored every record)), and the shared price token — all probe-owned automatics); composite statement order, fixed once here so the exact-diff gate checks it: (1) terminal check FIRST (after declaration-only statements with constant/default initialization and before every helper call, carry read other than probe_bSaved, sequence reservation, schema population, arithmetic, or emission; before schema, shadow arithmetic, provenance joins, or any other probe call): if probe_capped || probe_dead already true, emit nothing and perform no schema, sequence increment, shadow/provenance computation, or normal/failure-record emission, and FALL THROUGH past all probe work (no return, no unload — probe silence by latch only); else compare cap-exhaustion (`probe_seq >= PROBE_CAP`, never addition-based) — on cap-exhausted-before-reservation set probe_capped=true AND probe_dead=true BEFORE emitting, then emit the single STOPRESOLVE_CAP line (complete STOPRESOLVE CAP line per the P034 template, non-sequenced, carries no emitSeq, does not increment), and latch-and-continue through the guarded if / else-if / else-if / else chain (no return, no unload; latch-and-continue here means only that control resumes the live path after the probe block, never continuation into a later probe step — the run always completes the range; CAP is unreachable by bar count in a single uninterrupted tester execution in this envelope (s_lastBarTime and probe statics reset together on reinitialization; any reinitialization or multiple execution segment is recorded and fails the one-run equivalence unless expressly permitted) — cap-headroom bound: at most one C-reach per closed bar (3168 bars measured on the archive run, FRESHVETO-V1 G1), so the 20000 reservation cannot exhaust in one uninterrupted execution - retained strictly defensive; the 20001st reaching evaluation is the CAP evaluation (frozen semantics); (2) test probe_bSaved (arm selector between the BSAVE_FAIL and NORMAL arms; no sequence is reserved before this test) — the cap unit is every pre-terminal C-reaching evaluation (reserved sequences 1..20000): normal records carry theirs, BSAVE_FAIL carries its reserved sequence, and gaps in normal-record sequences are terminal-only (whole-run per-bar uniqueness additionally assumes monotonic tester-series progression with no reinitialization); (3) reserve the sequence inside the taken branch (increment-then-take: the increment executes first so BSAVE_FAIL and NORMAL both carry the next reserved sequence with gaps terminal-only, the first NORMAL carries emitSeq=1, and no ++/-- appears anywhere) after the arm-selecting probe_bSaved test and BEFORE any syntactic reference to any other bare carry — range fixed here: from the start of insertion C in raw source through the successful-branch boundary, with no macros containing carry identifiers anywhere in the build and no direct or indirect value read from any A/B carry through aliases, aggregate initializers, function arguments, references, or copied temporaries (the only permitted carry read before success is probe_bSaved; STAGE-1 asserts all, else halt; no preprocessed-token inspection is offered or required); on false set probe_dead=true BEFORE emitting, then emit the dedicated failure record type STOPRESOLVE_BSAVE_FAIL (complete STOPRESOLVE BSAVE_FAIL line per the P034 template — barTime is the L6607 parameter and dir is g_dir, both available at C; there is no `site` symbol at C, so the field carries the build-record string literal "S5"), and latch-and-continue through the guarded if / else-if / else-if / else chain (no return, no unload; latch-and-continue here means only that control resumes the live path after the probe block, never continuation into a later probe step); (3a) populate the value array with the constant-only "?" prefill (initialization, exempt from the ordering restriction below); (3b) populate the key array (38 key assignments in P034 field order, every NORMAL record, before SCHEMA - the array is automatic storage so step 6 rereads it per record); (4) emit STOPRESOLVE_SCHEMA once from the key array only, never the value array (complete STOPRESOLVE SCHEMA line per the P034 template — self-verifying count; unsequenced, carries no emitSeq; once-only via the probe_schema_done flag inside insertion C — guard, emit, then set true, no additional site; SCHEMA consumes the key array ONLY, never the value array, and NORMAL consumes both in matching indices — one key-array definition and one normal-value population site, asserted at STAGE-1; SCHEMA is metadata, not evidence that the normal-record path is valid — a broken A/B path emits no SCHEMA and terminates at step 3); (5) common serialization including probe_rLiveV plus branch-local shadow computation populating the named numeric/Boolean temporaries (declared in the common declaration region ahead of the chain; step (5) computes into them), initialized at declaration and populated only in the successful branch at this phase (explicit temp computation list, fixed here: double probe_slDistExt1 (shadow slDistExt1 = MathAbs(currentPrice - pxExt1)); double probe_rExt1v (DIAGNOSTIC quotient only: evaluated as tpDist / slDistExt1 solely when finite-input and denominator conditions hold (probe_shadowOk plus finite tpDist plus slDistExt1 > 0.0); otherwise its initialized value stays unused and serialization emits the authorized sentinel); bool probe_shadowOk (ext1Defined plus finite pxExt1 plus finite entryPx, with ext1Defined carried by the enclosing branch so the literal builds two validity conjuncts); bool probe_wouldGateV (LITERAL live-equivalent predicate retaining short-circuit behavior: (slDistExt1 > 0.0 && (tpDist / slDistExt1) >= gateConst), with NO added finite guard); double probe_extDistD (MathRound signed point displacement input); int probe_extSideI (strict side comparison result); double probe_rLiveV (live quotient result, validated before formatting); double probe_extRnd (rounded displacement, range-tested after rounding); double probe_extDifD (signed pre-division displacement, checked before dividing); entryPx/currentPrice share probe_tokPx; raw denominators shared where the packet states identity; shadow tpDist carried unchanged; formatting reads the temps, never serialized tokens); (5b) populate the value array (38 positions interleaved with computation: the datetime encoding/temp-reuse rule requires each temp/format result to store into probe_vals[i] in the next statement with reuse-before-store impossible; every other position receives its final value before NORMAL assembly and no scratch value is overwritten before its required consumers use it; syntactic counts and executed-path counts stay separate per P038); (6) NORMAL assembly: envelope initialized first (`probe_line = "[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=NORMAL";`) then a single index loop `for(int probe_i = 0; probe_i < 38; probe_i = probe_i + 1)` pairing keys with values in prefix-space form (`probe_line = probe_line + " " + probe_keys[probe_i] + "=" + probe_vals[probe_i];`, separator before each field so a trailing space is structurally unreachable), then one Print of probe_line (the SCHEMA assembler is the same i=0 counter form over keys only with comma separator per the frozen comma-separated names template - the one deliberate deviation from the NORMAL join, template-frozen). Frozen C insertion text (literal source; STAGE-1 exact-diff checks it verbatim - two store positions ride STAGE-1-bound as the sole bounded exception stated after the literal): `static uint probe_seq = 0; const uint PROBE_CAP = 20000; static bool probe_schema_done = false; static bool probe_capped = false; static bool probe_dead = false; string probe_keys[38]; string probe_vals[38]; string probe_line; string probe_tmpA; string probe_tokPx; double probe_slDistExt1 = -1e308; double probe_rExt1v = -1e308; bool probe_shadowOk = false; bool probe_wouldGateV = false; double probe_extDistD = 0.0; int probe_extSideI = -2147483647; double probe_rLiveV = -1e308; double probe_extRnd = 0.0; double probe_extDifD = 0.0; if(probe_capped || probe_dead) { } else if(probe_seq >= PROBE_CAP) { probe_capped = true; probe_dead = true; probe_line = "[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=CAP reservedTotal=20000 reason=CAP_EXHAUSTED"; Print(probe_line); } else if(!probe_bSaved) { probe_seq = probe_seq + 1; probe_dead = true; probe_tmpA = TimeToString(barTime, TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES); StringReplace(probe_tmpA, " ", "-"); probe_line = "[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=BSAVE_FAIL emitSeq=" + IntegerToString(probe_seq) + " probe_bSaved=0 barTime=" + probe_tmpA + " dir=" + IntegerToString((int)g_dir) + " site=S5"; Print(probe_line); } else { probe_seq = probe_seq + 1; for(int probe_j = 0; probe_j < 38; probe_j = probe_j + 1) probe_vals[probe_j] = "?"; probe_keys[0] = "barTime"; probe_keys[1] = "dir"; probe_keys[2] = "entryPx"; probe_keys[3] = "tpPx"; probe_keys[4] = "incomingSlRef"; probe_keys[5] = "liveSel"; probe_keys[6] = "slLive"; probe_keys[7] = "pxExt1"; probe_keys[8] = "ext1Defined"; probe_keys[9] = "ext1Imb"; probe_keys[10] = "rLive"; probe_keys[11] = "rExt1"; probe_keys[12] = "gateConst"; probe_keys[13] = "wouldGate"; probe_keys[14] = "vetoStateAtSite"; probe_keys[15] = "sessionUseAtSite"; probe_keys[16] = "ext1Slot"; probe_keys[17] = "ext1BarTime"; probe_keys[18] = "s0slot"; probe_keys[19] = "s0imb"; probe_keys[20] = "s1slot"; probe_keys[21] = "s1imb"; probe_keys[22] = "ladOriginPx"; probe_keys[23] = "ladOriginBarTime"; probe_keys[24] = "ladOriginSite"; probe_keys[25] = "extSideOk"; probe_keys[26] = "extDistPts"; probe_keys[27] = "rawNumLive"; probe_keys[28] = "rawDenLive"; probe_keys[29] = "rawNumExt1"; probe_keys[30] = "rawDenExt1"; probe_keys[31] = "wouldAdopt_monotone"; probe_keys[32] = "actualGate"; probe_keys[33] = "emitSeq"; probe_keys[34] = "currentPrice"; probe_keys[35] = "s0px"; probe_keys[36] = "s1px"; probe_keys[37] = "ladOriginStamp"; if(!probe_schema_done) { probe_line = "[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=SCHEMA fields=38 names="; for(int probe_i = 0; probe_i < 38; probe_i = probe_i + 1) { if(probe_i == 0) probe_line = probe_line + probe_keys[probe_i]; else probe_line = probe_line + "," + probe_keys[probe_i]; } Print(probe_line); probe_schema_done = true; } probe_tmpA = TimeToString(barTime, TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES); StringReplace(probe_tmpA, " ", "-"); probe_vals[0] = probe_tmpA; probe_vals[1] = IntegerToString((int)g_dir); if(!MathIsValidNumber(currentPrice)) { probe_vals[2] = "INVALID"; probe_vals[34] = "INVALID"; } else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", currentPrice); probe_vals[2] = probe_tokPx; probe_vals[34] = probe_tokPx; } if(!MathIsValidNumber(tpTarget)) probe_vals[3] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", tpTarget); probe_vals[3] = probe_tokPx; } if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_inSlRef)) probe_vals[4] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_inSlRef); probe_vals[4] = probe_tokPx; } probe_vals[5] = IntegerToString(probe_sel); if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_slLive)) probe_vals[6] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_slLive); probe_vals[6] = probe_tokPx; } if(!MathIsValidNumber(slDist) || !MathIsValidNumber(tpDist)) probe_vals[10] = "INVALID"; else { if(slDist > 0.0) probe_rLiveV = tpDist / slDist; if(slDist > 0.0 && MathIsValidNumber(probe_rLiveV)) probe_vals[10] = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_rLiveV); else if(slDist > 0.0) probe_vals[10] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[10] = "-"; } if(!MathIsValidNumber(InpMinRewardRisk)) probe_vals[12] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[12] = StringFormat("%.17g", InpMinRewardRisk); probe_vals[32] = (tpOk ? "1" : "0"); probe_vals[33] = IntegerToString(probe_seq); if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_s0px)) probe_vals[35] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_s0px); probe_vals[35] = probe_tokPx; } if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_s1px)) probe_vals[36] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_s1px); probe_vals[36] = probe_tokPx; } probe_vals[18] = IntegerToString(probe_s0slot); probe_vals[19] = IntegerToString(probe_s0imb); probe_vals[20] = IntegerToString(probe_s1slot); probe_vals[21] = IntegerToString(probe_s1imb); if(!MathIsValidNumber(g_sl41_oPx)) probe_vals[22] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", g_sl41_oPx); probe_vals[22] = probe_tokPx; } probe_tmpA = TimeToString(g_sl41_oBT, TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES); StringReplace(probe_tmpA, " ", "-"); probe_vals[23] = probe_tmpA; probe_vals[24] = g_sl41_oSite; probe_tmpA = TimeToString(g_sl41_oStamp, TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES); StringReplace(probe_tmpA, " ", "-"); probe_vals[37] = probe_tmpA; if(!MathIsValidNumber(tpDist)) probe_vals[27] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[27] = StringFormat("%.17g", tpDist); if(!MathIsValidNumber(slDist)) probe_vals[28] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[28] = StringFormat("%.17g", slDist); probe_vals[14] = "-"; probe_vals[15] = "-"; if(g_sl41_def == 1) { probe_shadowOk = (MathIsValidNumber(g_sl41_px) && MathIsValidNumber(currentPrice)); if(probe_shadowOk) probe_slDistExt1 = MathAbs(currentPrice - g_sl41_px); if(probe_shadowOk && MathIsValidNumber(tpDist) && probe_slDistExt1 > 0.0) probe_rExt1v = tpDist / probe_slDistExt1; probe_wouldGateV = (probe_slDistExt1 > 0.0 && (tpDist / probe_slDistExt1) >= InpMinRewardRisk); if(!MathIsValidNumber(g_sl41_px)) probe_vals[7] = "INVALID"; else { probe_tokPx = StringFormat("%.17g", g_sl41_px); probe_vals[7] = probe_tokPx; } probe_vals[8] = IntegerToString(g_sl41_def); probe_vals[9] = IntegerToString(g_sl41_imb); if(!probe_shadowOk || !MathIsValidNumber(tpDist) || !MathIsValidNumber(probe_slDistExt1) || !MathIsValidNumber(probe_rExt1v)) probe_vals[11] = "INVALID"; else { if(probe_slDistExt1 > 0.0) probe_vals[11] = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_rExt1v); else probe_vals[11] = "-"; } probe_vals[13] = (probe_wouldGateV ? "1" : "0"); probe_vals[16] = IntegerToString(g_sl41_slot); probe_tmpA = TimeToString(g_sl41_bt, TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES); StringReplace(probe_tmpA, " ", "-"); probe_vals[17] = probe_tmpA;  if(probe_shadowOk) { if(g_dir == DIR_LONG) probe_extSideI = ((g_sl41_px < currentPrice) ? 1 : 0); else if(g_dir == DIR_SHORT) probe_extSideI = ((g_sl41_px > currentPrice) ? 1 : 0); else probe_extSideI = -1; if(probe_extSideI < 0) probe_vals[25] = "-"; else probe_vals[25] = IntegerToString(probe_extSideI); if(probe_extSideI < 0) probe_vals[26] = "-"; else if(!MathIsValidNumber(_Point) || !(_Point > 0.0)) probe_vals[26] = "-"; else { if(g_dir == DIR_LONG) probe_extDifD = (currentPrice - g_sl41_px); else probe_extDifD = (g_sl41_px - currentPrice); if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_extDifD)) probe_vals[26] = "INVALID"; else { probe_extDistD = (probe_extDifD / _Point); if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_extDistD)) probe_vals[26] = "INVALID"; else { probe_extRnd = MathRound(probe_extDistD); if(!MathIsValidNumber(probe_extRnd) || MathAbs(probe_extRnd) > 99999.0) probe_vals[26] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[26] = DoubleToString(probe_extRnd, 0); } } } } else { probe_vals[25] = "-"; probe_vals[26] = "-"; }  if(!MathIsValidNumber(tpDist)) probe_vals[29] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[29] = StringFormat("%.17g", tpDist); if(!probe_shadowOk || !MathIsValidNumber(probe_slDistExt1)) probe_vals[30] = "INVALID"; else probe_vals[30] = StringFormat("%.17g", probe_slDistExt1); if(probe_shadowOk && (g_dir == DIR_LONG || g_dir == DIR_SHORT) && (probe_sel == 0 || probe_sel == 1) && MathIsValidNumber(probe_slLive) && MathIsValidNumber(currentPrice) && MathAbs(currentPrice - probe_slLive) != 0.0 && ((g_dir == DIR_LONG && probe_slLive < currentPrice) || (g_dir == DIR_SHORT && probe_slLive > currentPrice)) && ((g_dir == DIR_LONG && g_sl41_px < probe_slLive) || (g_dir == DIR_SHORT && g_sl41_px > probe_slLive))) probe_vals[31] = "1"; else probe_vals[31] = "0";  } else { probe_vals[7] = "-"; probe_vals[8] = IntegerToString(g_sl41_def); probe_vals[9] = "-999"; probe_vals[11] = probe_vals[10]; probe_vals[13] = (tpOk ? "1" : "0"); probe_vals[16] = "-999"; probe_vals[17] = "-"; probe_vals[25] = "-"; probe_vals[26] = "-"; probe_vals[29] = probe_vals[27]; probe_vals[30] = probe_vals[28]; probe_vals[31] = "0"; } probe_line = "[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=NORMAL"; for(int probe_i = 0; probe_i < 38; probe_i = probe_i + 1) probe_line = probe_line + " " + probe_keys[probe_i] + "=" + probe_vals[probe_i]; Print(probe_line); }` Two store positions (probe_vals[14]/probe_vals[15], veto/session site snapshots) ride STAGE-1-bound as the sole bounded exception: their exact landed symbols STAGE-1 names with scope proof (v18 rule kept); positions, strike behavior, and ledger maxima frozen here; only these two RHS bindings come from the build record rather than this page. Reads the carries plus candidate-local ext1/provenance from the g_sl41_* globals (EA L1112-L1117 declarations: g_sl41_def at L1112 with _px/_slot/_bt/_imb following through L1117 — kept textually separate from the L1108-11 origin family everywhere on this page; L5496-97 publish inside `bool ComputeSlReference`, S5-path call at EA L8779 inside EvaluateClosedBar before C — STAGE-1 asserts L8779 is the last ComputeSlReference exit before C on every C-reaching path with the full census cited (L5291 declaration; ComputeSlReference invocations at L6152 inside `bool SlRefMemo` (EA L6067) and L8779 S5; L7271 comment-only; SlRefMemo call sites L7273 S2POLL + L8406 S3ARM, none in L8779→L9670) plus the publication obligation (the L8779 invocation publishes the complete consumed g_sl41_* ext1 tuple for that invocation before successful return, including the undefined state and the halt state (sl41_halt != "-" rows publish with legacy - origin-price/origin-time fields) when applicable, with no subsequent writer before C proved as reach unconditional on the S5 path within the L5305 debug gate, whose effective value is asserted pre-run (no-earlier-return census L5291-L5494 on the S5 path; guard-state proof deleted per B-8), not source-line order alone, else halt; origin quadruple from g_sl41_oPx/g_sl41_oBT/g_sl41_oSite/g_sl41_oStamp (EA L1108-11) written on the S5 path at L8773-76 before L8779 — STAGE-1 gates run inputs to InpDebugLog=true plus the archive/run equivalence plus the 165-site global debug-input census, else halt; the printed ladOriginStamp must equal barTime offline (`ladOriginStamp != barTime ⇒ halt` — the single collapsed check under tester-envelope semantics (series cannot roll over mid-call in the tester; never carried unexamined to a live chart); no iTime call exists in the inserted C hunk and none is authorized there (neighbor iTime reads at EA L9727/L9741/L9770 are pre-existing same-block prints outside the hunks); both underlying values are bar-open datetimes with zero seconds by iTime bar-open semantics at L8776/L11210, so the minute-resolution serialized comparison is exact — labeled minute-resolution with this proof); the printed ladOrigin triple (STOPRESOLVE ladOriginSite = g_sl41_oSite solely) is joined offline against the same-bar SLEXT481 row (whose site is the L5489 local) with ordered-occurrence matching and multiplicity preserved plus required equality between the two site sources — a mismatch halts grading as stale-provenance; halt-state rows (sl41_halt != -) join-halt here (freshness only) (ext1 provenance matching applies to DEFINED rows only — all 442 SLEXT481 data rows in FRESHVETO-V1 are ext1Defined=1 with zero undefined-data-row counterexamples two-pattern-verified, so undefined rows grade stamp/site freshness only); direction is cast natively as (int)g_dir — no DirName call in the inserted C hunk (neighbor DirName reads at EA L9728/L9742/L9772 are pre-existing same-block prints outside the hunks); STAGE-1 asserts the build-record domain g_dir ∈ {DIR_LONG,DIR_SHORT} at C, halting otherwise); computes the ext1 shadow with an explicit pre-arithmetic branch (if ext1Defined: compute from pxExt1; else copy slDist/tpDist/rLive/actualGate — no sentinel ever enters arithmetic); shadow-distance construction and the literal wouldGate predicate below are exceptions to the finite-gated diagnostic-arithmetic rule: they use the actual numeric operands, never display tokens; finite checks govern diagnostic formatting and acceptance, never substitution or guarding of the mirror; "printed independently" in P034/P036 specifies formatting precedence within the single record, not separate emissions. Emits. NOTE stated plainly: there is NO unload request and NO early return anywhere in the probe — no executable ExpertRemove call appears in the inserted hunks on this page; probe silence after a terminal record comes from the latches structurally, never from unload timing; the tick pipeline always runs to completion, so the actual-path archive comparison is never voided by probe behavior and a bSaved failure costs probe evidence only. Rationale (measured on disk 2026-09-18): the L9626 block closes at L9666, so in-block declarations die before C — carries live outside it; s1x_* symbols all die at L9666, hence the B saves; slDist/tpDist are computed L9668-L9669, hence emission at C; the occupying recorder block (L9671 comment through L9779 close, pasted in the relay) already sits post-gate with s1e_-prefixed locals (s1o_/s1q_ live further down at L9784-L9823, named here so the audit's reach is explicit) — C's probe_-prefixed storage is collision-disjoint by prefix over the whole EvaluateClosedBar body plus file-scope globals (probe_ occurs zero times on the landed tree — STAGE-1 re-asserts, else halt; a pre-existing nested probe_* declaration would shadow silently, so the audit is whole-body, never neighborhood-only). Closure L9666, gate L9670, and everything downstream untouched; existing live statements unchanged. Volume invariant, frozen here: one NORMAL-or-terminal probe record for each non-dead C-reaching evaluation (plus the separately permitted once-only SCHEMA metadata record on the first successful evaluation); dead/capped short-circuit evaluations emit nothing. Terminal cardinality: zero or one terminal record total per run; if present its type is exactly one of CAP or BSAVE_FAIL; non-probe diagnostics after terminal latch/emission never count as probe emission. BSAVE_FAIL is the ONLY terminal path that can occur before SCHEMA (a first-reaching bSaved failure emits only BSAVE_FAIL — instrument-failure class, run void); a CAP terminal can occur only after the 20000th reserved NORMAL record with SCHEMA already emitted exactly once (CAP without preceding SCHEMA plus 20000 contiguous NORMAL records is structurally invalid output as well as a failed run).

slLive, gateConst, currentPrice, and actualGate are OBSERVED live values at C (slLive = probe_slLive; gateConst = InpMinRewardRisk as consumed by the L9670 test; currentPrice read directly; actualGate = tpOk, preserved literally without modification). rLive is the quotient recomputed by identical pure arithmetic over the observed live operands slDist/tpDist (same numbers, same ops — no unknown inputs, labeled as recomputed display; a printed wouldGate=1 with a non-finite evaluated live quotient can likewise arise from division overflow with finite operands, and finite raw tokens do not establish live-quotient validity). pxExt1 is the STOPRESOLVE field carrying the candidate-local slExt1 read; rExt1 is the shadow ratio over shadow operands constructed by the packet-stated identical formula (shadow slDistExt1 = MathAbs(currentPrice - pxExt1), exactly as slDist from slRef; tpDist unchanged; extDistPts stays a separate diagnostic and is never substituted here). wouldGate is the literal evaluation of the COMPLETE L9670 predicate over the constructed shadow operands — `(slDistExt1 > 0.0 && (tpDist / slDistExt1) >= gateConst)` with identical short-circuit semantics and NO added finite guard (the exact live-equivalent mirror): the printed Boolean is never clamped, never derived from a formatted field or sentinel on shadowOk-true rows (literal on valid shadow operands); on shadowOk-false rows probe_wouldGateV evaluates over the poison sentinel and its printed 0 is unavailable for grading per the P036 undecided class, never a faithful mirror (a faithful true on a non-finite quotient exposes a live-predicate hazard as a SEPARATE acceptance failure — never a silent guard, never blamed on the probe; the run still fails (a printed wouldGate=1 with a non-finite evaluated quotient can arise from a positive-infinite numerator or from division overflow with finite operands and a finite positive denominator; finite raw tokens therefore do not establish quotient validity; either case fails acceptance with the literal Boolean preserved; !shadowOk rows print structural 0 and NaN >= 1.0 is false). Validity is handled separately from the mirror in four explicit classes (no live code touched): live-input validity, live-quotient validity, shadow-input/quotient validity, diagnostic availability — Booleans preserved literally, acceptance classified independently: non-finite shadow inputs (or a non-finite constructed shadow distance) print INVALID for the unavailable counterfactual fields per P036 and fail acceptance explicitly as a non-finite-operand failure — this is the express exception to literal-result grading, stated here, never invented at build; wouldGate=0 with any INVALID operand relevant to that calculation is classed undecided — never a gate fail, never a prediction match; prediction classification reads undecided while run acceptance reads fail (an unrelated invalid diagnostic never reclassifies a finite gate calculation); a non-finite EVALUATED live quotient is an independent acceptance failure with literal actualGate preserved (finite denominator-guard blocking, where rLive='-' and the quotient is not evaluated, stays valid). rLive/rExt1 describe ratios where defined and neither denotes the complete gate. With ext1 undefined, shadow operands and gate result equal the actual-path operands and gate result (copying occurs before validity classification: any INVALID live/shadow operand relevant to the calculation makes the copied Boolean undecided (shadow) or an independent invalid-operand failure (live actualGate path, including an actualGate=true copy) under the same policy; actualGate itself is always the literal already-computed Boolean with no finite guard retroactively imposed); undefined-ext1 records are FALLBACK-CLASS ONLY — excluded from ext1 shadow/gate prediction grading and source-change conclusions; grade only that the copied fields equal their live counterparts and that ext1 sentinels are correct. vetoStateAtSite and sessionUseAtSite are site-readable state snapshots at C — symbol identity is a builder-disk precondition: STAGE-1 names the exact symbols (tpPx prints tpTarget — confirmed here as the mapping; entryPx prints currentPrice itself — the S5 entry reference per the L8751/L8753 lines, same value by construction from the single token probe_tokPx, and every row must print them textually equal as a schema/duplication invariant only (both fields populate from probe_tokPx; proves serialization consistency, never mapping or runtime value; the ladOriginPx comparison stays the real check) — a non-finite currentPrice is a mandatory live-input failure regardless of textual equality; archived TP_ELECT entry stays a separate offline operand, never a probe field) or strikes the field — vetoStateAtSite/sessionUseAtSite ONLY (prints '-', ordering claims drop accordingly; the '-' token is explicitly authorized for these two strikable fields, overriding the closed-enum rejection rule for strike rows only; ladOriginSite '-' stays a stale-halt, never a strike token; strike substitution is spelled once here: the base literal carries probe_vals[14] = "-"; and probe_vals[15] = "-"; inside the success arm, and the STAGE-1 addendum hunk overwrites those two statements with the named landed-symbol bindings; each addendum files the complete RHS expression, source type, encoding/domain, maximum width, and any permitted formatter call; the purity allow-list and no-live-reference-mutation rule apply to those expressions explicitly; if that cannot be established the literal "-" strike stands; no new getter or helper is authorized; each addendum store is exactly one assignment statement with no guard and no branch — if a guard or branch is required the "-" strike stands; each bound RHS is a read-only expression over the named site-readable symbols, constants, and permitted formatters, with no nested assignment, increment/decrement, or mutation of any other probe storage; only probe_vals[14] and [15] are mutable C-text positions, and any other difference from the pasted literal invalidates the exact-diff gate; a strike is deletion of the addendum (no grading-side code substitution, never probe code)); never downstream outcomes and never execution proof. Use the existing inline quotient form identically, preserving guard/short-circuit behavior. Every STOPRESOLVE-family line opens with the fixed envelope `[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=NORMAL|SCHEMA|CAP|BSAVE_FAIL` (house tag included; the type discriminator follows the common prefix; envelope excluded from the fields=38 payload count; common envelope shape on all four types; all other envelope descriptions on this page defer byte-for-byte to this order). Parser transport rule, frozen here: strip the terminal's documented timestamp/thread prefix ONLY (exact form documented from the day-log tail at STAGE-1), then require the literal `[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE` open — stripping arbitrary text until STOPRESOLVE appears is forbidden. Each normal (type=NORMAL) record carries, with its emitSeq, the following 38 payload fields in order: barTime, dir, entryPx, tpPx, incomingSlRef (= probe_inSlRef source; named here once; defined as slRef as read at the A site pre-L9618 (provable only under the filed manifest: the L8780-L9626 slRef census with InpAdoptExt1=false)), liveSel, slLive, pxExt1, ext1Defined, ext1Imb, rLive, rExt1, gateConst, wouldGate, vetoStateAtSite, sessionUseAtSite, ext1Slot, ext1BarTime, s0slot, s0imb, s1slot, s1imb, ladOriginPx, ladOriginBarTime, ladOriginSite, extSideOk, extDistPts, rawNumLive, rawDenLive, rawNumExt1, rawDenExt1, wouldAdopt_monotone, actualGate, emitSeq, currentPrice, s0px, s1px, ladOriginStamp. EmitSeq appears exactly once at position 34 of 38; ladOriginStamp is position 38. Field contract table (frozen; derived transcription of the rules above, no new rule - field:kind:max:sentinel-or-domain): barTime:DT:16:tmpA; dir:INT:2:1/-1; entryPx:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; tpPx:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; incomingSlRef:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; liveSel:INT:2:99-halts (99 forbidden; offline poison rule halts grading); slLive:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; pxExt1:NUM:24:-for-undef/INVALID; ext1Defined:INT:1:0/1; ext1Imb:INT:4:-999-undef; rLive:NUM:24:-/INVALID; rExt1:NUM:24:-/INVALID; gateConst:NUM:24:anticipated-1/INVALID; wouldGate:BOOL:1:0/1; vetoStateAtSite:STR:STAGE-1-split:-strike; sessionUseAtSite:STR:STAGE-1-split:-strike; ext1Slot:INT:4:-999-undef; ext1BarTime:DT:16:-for-undef; s0slot:INT:4:slot; s0imb:INT:2:imb; s1slot:INT:4:slot; s1imb:INT:2:imb; ladOriginPx:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; ladOriginBarTime:DT:16:tmpA; ladOriginSite:STR:6:-for-stale-halt; extSideOk:INT:1:0/1/-; extDistPts:INT:7:DoubleToString-m0/INVALID; rawNumLive:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; rawDenLive:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; rawNumExt1:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; rawDenExt1:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; wouldAdopt_monotone:BOOL:1:0/1; actualGate:BOOL:1:0/1; emitSeq:INT:5:seq; currentPrice:NUM:24:%.17g/INVALID; s0px:NUM:24:0-when-slot-minus-1/INVALID; s1px:NUM:24:0-when-slot-minus-1/INVALID; ladOriginStamp:DT:16:tmpA. walkEnd NOT added for this build (B-2: capturing exit reasons expands B beyond assignment-only and revises schema/transport gates; the 39th-field slot stays empty with the B-6 publication-stamp alternative carried alongside walkEnd for the live relay; council disposes). The three non-normal wire templates, frozen here (each shows the envelope once with its complete ordered payload under the single type= discriminator (STOPRESOLVE plus type=NORMAL/SCHEMA/CAP/BSAVE_FAIL; the underscore spellings STOPRESOLVE_CAP, STOPRESOLVE_SCHEMA and STOPRESOLVE_BSAVE_FAIL wherever they appear in this packet are prose shorthand for the STOPRESOLVE + type=CAP/SCHEMA/BSAVE_FAIL records respectively, never wire tokens; fields and names are SCHEMA metadata after the common envelope, never NORMAL payload and never common-envelope keys)): SCHEMA delivers the complete line `[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=SCHEMA fields=38 names=<38 comma-separated payload keys in order>`; CAP delivers the complete line `[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=CAP reservedTotal=20000 reason=CAP_EXHAUSTED`; BSAVE_FAIL delivers the complete line `[SRJ-EA] STOPRESOLVE format=2 pkt=PACKET_EXT1LIVE-001-v26 base=6C2E4028 type=BSAVE_FAIL emitSeq=<reserved> probe_bSaved=0 barTime=<encoded> dir=<native-int> site=S5`. Angle-bracket terms above are substitutions, not wire characters. Line grammar, frozen here and authoritative for P036 (which states field-level policies only): one line per record; fixed key=value order per the field list; single ASCII space (0x20) between fields; no spaces inside encoded values; no trailing whitespace before EOL (each record line ends with the last value byte, then the line terminator); closed-enum strings must be printable ASCII (0x21-0x7E) with no whitespace, line terminators, or non-ASCII (explicit domain condition on ladOriginSite, vetoStateAtSite, sessionUseAtSite, and the BSAVE_FAIL site literal; rejection (at build for literals; run-time source/domain binding plus offline parser rejection for runtime-sourced strings) if any enumerated string violates it; a - in ladOriginSite is a stale-global/default halt (g_sl41_oSite initialised to - at EA L1110), never a sentinel, and is excluded from the closed enum); out-of-domain values are rejected, never silently re-encoded at build; datetimes encoded space-free as TimeToString(TIME_DATE|TIME_MINUTES) with the interior space replaced by '-' via StringReplace on a probe-owned temp (assign TimeToString to probe_tmpA, call StringReplace(temp," ","-"), serialize temp into probe_vals[i] in the next statement — the temps' only mutation, allow-listed as writes to probe-owned storage); Boolean fields as 0/1; dir prints (int)g_dir natively as a decimal integer with accepted domain exactly {1,-1} on every record type carrying dir (NORMAL and BSAVE_FAIL alike; 0 is recognizable but invalid and fails acceptance everywhere; a BSAVE_FAIL row carrying dir 0 reports the domain violation as instrument-failure evidence, never reclassified; no crosswalk table; no DirName call in the inserted C hunk (neighbor DirName reads at EA L9728/L9742/L9772 are pre-existing same-block prints outside the hunks)); ext1Defined prints the raw producer int with the {0,1} domain asserted at build — no truthy value is ever silently collapsed); a stale/corrupt 2 prints ext1Defined=2 on a FALLBACK-CLASS row before the domain halt (record-class assignment precedes the check - stated here). integers as decimal; prices and numerics per the numeric acceptance grammar `^-?(\d+\.?\d*|\.\d+)([eE][+-]?\d+)?$` (negative zero accepted as binary64 round-trip; exponent signs including `+` accepted — canonical is defined per field type (field-typed rule, governing here): binary64 prices, raw operands, and ratios must byte-equal StringFormat("%.17g", parsed-value) as the raw wire spelling; the offline reference formatter (implementation named in the build record) may exponent-normalize solely for its independent comparison; noncanonical raw tokens are rejected; integer fields and Boolean encodings must byte-equal canonical decimal syntax within their domains; extDistPts must byte-equal DoubleToString(m,0) after finite/range validation; sentinels must byte-equal their exact field-authorized tokens; the log-readback parser validates EVERY token against its own field rule, not a sample); sentinels as exact tokens '-' (guard-blocked/unavailable), -999 (absent ext1 integer IDs plus undefined ext1Imb), INVALID (failed field-validity check, including non-finite input/intermediate/result or the explicitly authorized extDistPts range failure); no quoting anywhere. Parse failures halting grading: noncanonical nan/inf spellings, grouping separators, interior whitespace, empty token, stray ? prefill token, reserialization mismatch. Text identifier fields (ladOriginSite plus the BSAVE_FAIL site literal) come from closed enum sets with the exact strings enumerated in the build record plus rejection/encoding rules for any outside value (STAGE-1 files them — page clearance does not call the grammar complete until it does); dir is exclusively a decimal integer with domain {1,-1}. Imbalance adjacency note (read here, where parsing happens): s0imb/s1imb print post-cast -1-style values while ext1Imb prints -999 when undefined and {-1,0,1,2,3} on defined rows (-1 means slot populated but the imbalance ReadFlow failed, benign and expected) — two encodings in adjacent fields, never joined without conversion. rawDenLive IS slDist and rawDenExt1 IS slDistExt1 (one identity clause — same quantities under the raw names, no new fields beyond the 38). Evaluations never reaching C emit nothing — S5 presence/absence comes from existing S5 diagnostics (17:00 included), never inferred from STOPRESOLVE absence. probe_bSaved prints only on BSAVE_FAIL (probe_bSaved=0 — the P032 step-3 branch; NORMAL records carry no probe_bSaved field (dropped for headroom, Opus-F-11/B-5)). Every NORMAL line must contain exactly the 38 payload keys in the specified order — no duplicates, omissions, or unknown keys — plus the exact envelope keys. No NORMAL row may carry any poison token in any field (-2147483647 in the four int carries, the canonical %.17g rendering of -1e308 in the three price carries (s0px/s1px/slLive), 99 in liveSel; match the STAGE-1-filed token for the poison rendering, never the source constant literally); any hit halts grading as incomplete-or-crossed B (offline poison rule; the micro-check line is sized 1056 poison-inclusive as ledger sizing; RECON47 measured the sink cap at 537 total (~489 payload), so falsifier survival holds only within the cap). Offline analysis additionally (a) derives liveSel from the printed s0/s1 inputs per the L9662-L9663 predicates — a derived-vs-saved disagreement halts grading with operands (the packet's code model falsified); (b) requires liveSel=-1 records to print incomingSlRef == slLive PLUS the universal carry identities as mandatory checks on every row: probe_sel=0 ⇒ slLive==s0px with saved slot/imb the s0 tuple; probe_sel=1 ⇒ slLive==s1px with saved slot/imb the s1 tuple (identical by construction — mismatch halts grading as crossed-assignment failure; the witness detects omission, these identities detect crossing); (c) requires the operand-mapping identities conditionally by record class: defined-finite rows reconstruct and compare all three (rawDenLive == MathAbs(currentPrice - slLive), rawNumLive == MathAbs(tpPx - currentPrice), rawDenExt1 == MathAbs(currentPrice - pxExt1)) as bit-equal reconstructions; undefined-fallback rows require shadow/live raw-pair equality plus ratio equality plus gate equality with the prescribed sentinels; the reference-arithmetic validation includes signed-zero subtraction and absolute-value cases reproducing the compiler MathAbs behavior for negative zero; invalid-operand rows take the validity-failure classification with no arithmetic on display tokens; live-operand identities stay universal wherever finite reconstruction is defined (mismatch halts grading as crossed-wiring failure); A-siting itself is proven only by the build diff, never by any runtime witness. (d) requires the same-bar SIDE1E/SIDE1X cross-checks as mandatory on every row, with the external-falsifier claim scoped honestly: liveSl/liveStop at five decimals and livePass == actualGate exact Boolean are genuinely external (live-storage-derived); s0px/s1px at five-decimal printed precision plus s0slot/s1slot/s0imb/s1imb/sel exact integer equality are copy-consistency checks (shared walk implementation, downgraded per N-1 - the separate-producer check is the offline SLEXT481 join at EA L5485-L5493); liveR vs rLive by guard-state-first comparison: if blocked, require probe - and legacy 0.00 (EA L9747 legacy fallback prints 0.00 via 2dp); otherwise compare the finite quotient through the legacy formatter; neither token represents a failed finite check (mismatch halts grading as externally-wrong carries). barTime prints the L6607 function parameter. r0/r1 legacy collision noted (EA L9721-L9722 return 0.0 for both no-candidate and real zero ratio); rExt1 does not mirror that idiom (prints - per P036) (N-5). No assignment to the live path. AdoptOff held, OrderSend 0. Live activation only via later dual-key plus tokens.

Field definitions (diagnostic, not a validity guard; serialization grammar authoritative in P034 — this section states field-level policies only): rawNumLive/rawDenLive are the observed live tpDist/slDist; rawNumExt1/rawDenExt1 are tpDist/slDistExt1 as constructed above. Emission-before-validity split: raw operands and probe price fields are formatted in compiler-canonical round-trip form before validity substitution (single emission per record; first is formatting precedence within one record, never separate emissions); the INVALID token substitutes only where the finite check fails; arithmetic and ratio fields are gated on finite inputs — except shadow-distance construction and the literal wouldGate predicate, which are the stated exceptions using actual numeric operands, never display tokens; invalid-input rows are outside mirror-result equivalence (when probe_shadowOk is false the defined-branch predicate evaluates over the poison distance and its printed 0 is unavailable, never a faithful mirror - offline undecided class). Concretely: finite raw operands print lossless numeric text with 17 significant digits (canonical = byte-exact `StringFormat("%.17g", x)` output confirmed against the compiler, and a sample emission validated against the P034 grammar with locale-independent '.' and no thousands separators — else halt; validation set covers exponent, negative-zero, and boundary round-trip cases; the log-readback parser (not the EA formatter) independently verifies ASCII '.' only, no grouping, canonical reserialization with exponent normalization (strip leading exponent zeros to a minimum of two digits on both sides before comparison; one actual MQL5 %.17g exponent sample filed at STAGE-1; live magnitudes in [1e-4, 1e2] never exponentiate, but raw/shadow distance operands reach 1e-5 and below so the exponent path is run-reachable for rawNum/rawDen fields; exponent normalization is mandatory on actual records, never fixtures-only; STAGE-1 additionally files the compiler-compatible raw-token reconstruction rule (exponent width/case/sign and signed-zero behavior) and reference normalization must never pass a noncanonical raw spelling; extDistPts is an integer-valued-double diagnostic governed exclusively by its DoubleToString(m,0) field rule: -0 is accepted only when compiler-canonical under the filed formatter behavior, read numerically as zero with wire spelling preserved; the IntegerToString-style canonical rule governs actual integer fields, never this diagnostic), and field-typed canonical checks for EVERY token (binary64 prices, raw operands, and ratios by the %.17g reference; integer fields and Boolean encodings by canonical decimal syntax plus domains; extDistPts by DoubleToString(m,0) with finite/range validation; sentinels by exact field-authorized tokens; no-candidate prices print the canonical %.17g rendering of positive zero (`0`) paired with slot -1 (s0px/s1px only), never a sentinel and never '-'); pre-build synthetic fixtures (script-type; four templates; boundary formatter cases; worst-case line transport; ordinary-maximal plus poison-inclusive fixtures each with actual generated length) are read back from the actual script log; post-run every actual probe record is parsed against the frozen grammar (synthetic fixtures are never strategy-run observations; actual records need not attain worst-case widths)); non-finite operands or ratios print the single fixed token INVALID; zero-denominator guarded ratios print '-'; table/display prices stay 5 (prerequisite: filed legacy _Digits==5 for the frozen symbol; comparisons run through the filed legacy _Digits formatter - a contrary filed value revises the fixed-five-decimal claims by packet amendment, never silently); probe price fields (entryPx, tpPx, pxExt1, slLive, incomingSlRef, currentPrice, s0px, s1px, ladOriginPx) print with the same compiler-canonical round-trip form — printed independently of ratio-field guard state, still INVALID on its own finite-check failure, including the raw pairs (STAGE-1 exposure gate: the builder form must expose these read-only at C; a builder needing modification or guessed reconstruction halts the build — a struck raw-pair is NOT an acceptable reduced scope, the gate halts by design since these four fields are the degenerate answer); with ext1 undefined the shadow raw pair equals the live raw pair. Offline parsing follows the frozen P034 grammar exactly. extSideOk and extDistPts compute ONLY after ext1Defined plus finite pxExt1 plus finite entryPx hold — otherwise '-'; extSideOk keeps the 0/1/- domain and wouldAdopt_monotone keeps 0/1 - neither ever serializes as INVALID (disambiguation: DIR_NONE rows join dir=0 as instrument failure; the `else probe_extSideI = -1;` arm is dead under the P038 g_dir-in-{DIR_LONG,DIR_SHORT} domain assertion, kept as defence, so no gradeable dir=0 rows are expected; shadowOk-false rows join pxExt1 INVALID as unavailable counterfactual); INVALID applies only to the named fields permitting it (raw/ratio/counterfactual fields per P034/P036) (A5); extSideOk is strict price-side comparison vs entryPx (which equals currentPrice — the FLAG's currentPrice-based visibility therefore survives anything). Ratio fields print '-' where the denominator guard prevents division (no numeric ratio exists); '-' denotes a valid denominator-guard-blocked division, never a generic arithmetic failure (precedence: INVALID = failed finite check including failed intermediate checks after availability is established (non-finite subtraction, non-finite point quotient, out-of-range rounding); unavailable _Point (non-finite or non-positive) authorizes a third - cause on extDistPts with extSideOk unaffected; '-' = guard-blocked finite division; the three INVALID causes share one INVALID token and are indistinguishable on the wire, so cause diagnosis is disk-only). wouldGate comes from the literal mirror over constructed operands, never from a formatted field or sentinel; wouldGate=1 on a non-finite/invalid ratio is a separate acceptance failure (run fails, probe not blamed); wouldGate=0 with any INVALID operand relevant to that calculation is undecided. ext1Slot prints the candidate-local producer slot g_sl41_slot (ladder index, not a rung count and not s1x_s); domain [0, barShift+SRJ_LAD_ABS_SLOT_CAP] on defined rows (defined ext1 requires a real ladder slot); -999 on undefined rows; -999 or -1 on a defined row is halt-with-operands. s0imb/s1imb print post-cast ints with domain {-1,0,1,2,3} (-1 initial/unread; 0/1/2/3 flow codes per FL133-139; EA L9679 cites the older 122-127 lines with 0/1/2). extDistPts is protective-positive both directions — LONG: (entryPx-pxExt1)/_Point, SHORT: (pxExt1-entryPx)/_Point, via MathRound (the EA's existing primitive, cf. L5469) printed via DoubleToString(m,0) without decimals; the rounded double is range-tested against the filed |extDistPts| <= 99999 range before the offline (int) interpretation — out-of-range prints INVALID — positive = protective-side displacement, zero = rounded at-entry, negative = non-protective-side displacement. extSideOk=0 rows are listed separately in the run report; the sub-point boundary joint reading is explicit: protective-but-sub-point prints extSideOk=1 with extDistPts=0 while exact at-entry prints 0 with 0 — distinguished by the lossless prints, tied to currentPrice. wouldAdopt_monotone compares against slLive and is 1 only for a defined, FINITE pxExt1 with a VALID incumbent under strict directional comparison (SHORT: pxExt1 higher; LONG: pxExt1 lower) — read strictly as monotone RISK EXPANSION (adversity), never stop tightening; valid incumbent means liveSel in {0,1} (selector-fired) AND slLive finite AND protective-side vs currentPrice (labeled probe-local side definition, never the live SlimbProtectiveSideOk predicate (tie handling, _Point tolerance, and DIR_NONE handling inside the live helper are unknown here; helper equivalence remains deferred); labeled so no future reader infers the selector can produce non-protective incumbents) AND MathAbs(currentPrice-slLive) nonzero AND currentPrice itself finite; liveSel=-1 (incoming retained, validity unprovable at this site) is invalid for this comparison and prints 0 (an invalid incumbent is never treated as zero; this answers neither non-null nor gate-passed — it is this explicit predicate; read the 0 strictly as not-adopt-or-undecidable, with liveSel joined offline for the reason). The flag is REPORTED, not graded: no value of it constitutes a miss; it informs the monotone question window-locally for named rows observed at C (a named row missing at C leaves its monotone question unproved, never 0-by-default). Record-class rule: undefined-ext1 rows are FALLBACK-CLASS; halt-state rows are JOIN-HALT-CLASS, identified ONLY by the exact legacy origin-field pattern at EA L5487-L5488 (origin price AND origin time both print -; the equivalence to sl41_halt != - is established by EA L5487-L5488, not by an independently observed halt field; inconsistent partial patterns (one - plus one real value) are rejected and halt; classification is separate from ext1Defined: undefined rows copy live values, defined JOIN-HALT rows follow the defined shadow construction but are excluded from provenance-dependent prediction/source conclusions (grade stamp/site freshness only, never printed-precision price equality) (excluded from provenance-dependent predictions and source conclusions; undefined rows retain fallback copy-equality checks, defined JOIN-HALT rows retain defined-shadow arithmetic and Boolean self-consistency checks); the origin quadruple (ladOriginPx/ladOriginBarTime/ladOriginSite/ladOriginStamp) prints on every NORMAL record including undefined rows (ext1Defined already marks the case — suppressing staleness evidence where stale globals most likely survive buys nothing); ext1 sentinels on undefined rows: pxExt1/extSideOk/extDistPts '-', ext1Slot/ext1Imb -999, ext1BarTime '-', wouldAdopt_monotone 0, rExt1 = rLive, rawNumExt1/rawDenExt1 = live raw pair, wouldGate = actualGate (literal copy, subject to the validity-classification precedence above); display sentinels are never compared as valid R. entryPx is never struck (it prints currentPrice — never strikable; a non-finite currentPrice prints INVALID as a live-input failure); the P042 mandatory recompute fields (currentPrice, slLive, tpPx, gateConst) are EXCLUDED from the strike allowance entirely (a mandatory check never goes ungradeable by strike); the consolidated strike policy lives in P042.

