r); post-insertion full-file SHA256 filed in the build record; strike list filed in the same build record BEFORE the build (each struck sub-clause named — a post-run reader never guesses; mandatory-recompute fields never struck); exact-diff = insertions A+B+C literal source text, except the two explicitly named STAGE-1-bound RHS expressions, with diff-shape (the frozen C statement list below plus the named two-statement addendum hunk is the audited artifact; what is cleared is what compiles) (ten initialized declarations at A: one live copy + one false witness + eight poison values; eight carry saves plus bSaved=true — nine statements — at B; C declarations: 4 statics + 1 automatic const (PROBE_CAP) + string probe_keys[38] + string probe_vals[38] + probe_line + nine successful-branch numeric/Boolean temps (double probe_slDistExt1 + double probe_rExt1v + bool probe_shadowOk + bool probe_wouldGateV + double probe_extDistD + int probe_extSideI + double probe_rLiveV + double probe_extRnd + double probe_extDifD, initialized at declaration, populated only in the successful branch at P032 step 5) + probe_tmpA (single datetime temp, interleaved encode-store per P032 step 5b; both-referenced gate dropped with probe_tmpB) + probe_tokPx with 38 key assignments (frozen step 3b, every NORMAL record) and 38 value positions each with exactly one final population per emitted NORMAL record path after prefill, via 50 position-populations across the branch structure (26 common including 2 STAGE-1-bound + 12 defined + 12 fallback); syntactic store-statement counts STAGE-1-filed by mechanical count of the frozen literal: 38 key stores (probe_keys[0..37] once each), 78 value stores (40 common including the 2 STAGE-1-bound + 26 defined-branch + 12 fallback-branch), 1 prefill statement (probe_vals[probe_j] = "?"); three index loops: two `for(int probe_i = 0; probe_i < 38; probe_i = probe_i + 1)` — one over keys for SCHEMA (comma arm per the frozen names template), one over keys+values for NORMAL (prefix-space arm) - plus one prefill `for(int probe_j = 0; probe_j < 38; probe_j = probe_j + 1)` over values with "?"; four emission Prints — SCHEMA, NORMAL, CAP, BSAVE_FAIL, one per branch; NO return and NO ExpertRemove anywhere in the hunks); definite-assignment assertion re-derived against the actual enclosing code (loop census L8779→L9670: six loops L9051/L9218/L9230/L9368/L9386/L9506 all closed before the L9532 straight-line tail, sole loop to C is the L9632 inner walk with break/continue inside; EvaluateClosedBar invocation census: sole caller OnTick L11214 with (1,currentBarTime); A-site and C-site brace depth identical with no conditional/switch boundary between them; no return or other exit bypasses B inside the selector block; no intervening reassignment of the carries); lexical purity assertion over the hunks (writes allowed ONLY to named probe-owned storage — including the StringReplace datetime temps, the shared price token, and the key/value arrays; output/format/math helpers allow-listed as Print, PrintFormat (superset; PrintFormat unused in the hunks), StringFormat, DoubleToString, IntegerToString, TimeToString, StringReplace, MathAbs, MathRound, MathIsValidNumber — no wildcard, no iTime, no DirName, no reference parameters pointing at live state; no mutation through calls/references otherwise; no ++/--; NO termination-request call and NO early return exist in the probe — silence is latch-structural; zero references to the nine non-witness A carries before the successful probe_bSaved branch (references to probe_bSaved itself are permitted for the test and failure reporting) in raw source from the start of insertion C through the successful-branch boundary, with no macros containing carry identifiers anywhere in the build); unconditional no-footprint invariant (no strategy-state write, no selector/gate operand substitution, no change to existing strategy control flow, no unload request — NONE suspended, because the probe performs none); no-wri