extSideOk<=1; extDistPts<=7; rawNumLive<=24; rawDenLive<=24; rawNumExt1<=24; rawDenExt1<=24; wouldAdopt_monotone<=1; actualGate<=1; emitSeq<=5; currentPrice<=24; s0px<=24; s1px<=24; ladOriginStamp<=16; integer domains: dir in {1,-1}, liveSel in {-1,0,1}, gates in {0,1}, ext1Defined in {0,1}, ext1Imb in {-999,-1,0,1,2,3}, ext1Slot in {-999} u [0, barShift+SRJ_LAD_ABS_SLOT_CAP] (-1 halts on defined rows); s0slot/s1slot in 4-char ladder indices, s0imb/s1imb in {-1,0,1,2,3}, extDistPts in |x|<=99999, emitSeq in 1..20000; a print wider than its filed maximum halts grading with operands as ungraded shape, never silently absorbed; STAGE-1 halts unless the filed per-field maxima table widths fit the 30-char budget; the micro-check synthetic line is built 1056 from the filed maxima ledger; RECON47 measured the sink cap at 537 total (~489 payload), so the fixture demonstrates ledger arithmetic, never sink transport of full rows, and full-row grading is withheld past the cap while the 1024 figure holds single authoritative status as a conservative bound over the specified field domains (1024 is the normal ledger bound, 1056 the prefilled-poison rejection bound, neither a demonstrated sink length; RECON47 measured the sink cap at 537 total) (coupled: a domain violation in any raw-printed integer (ext1Defined, ladOriginSite, ext1Imb, ext1Slot, s0/s1 imb/slot carries, dir, liveSel, extDistPts, none clamped at build) can exceed the filed ceiling, so ceiling proof and domain halt stand or fall together; the offline over-width halt catches all of them), subject to compiler-format validation (never estimate-grade); arity failure (a line without exactly the 38 ordered payload keys plus the exact envelope keys) is the graded transport falsifier in the transport-halt class, never a grading miss; rows cut by the measured sink cap grade on the present prefix (positions 0-22 plus full SCHEMA); keys past the cut are withheld, never failed; tester-log sink equivalence asserted by name (post-