ust not warn — if the compiler flags anything at the hunks, the design choice fails this gate and halts with the compiler output filed (known gate risk filed here: the empty if(probe_capped || probe_dead) { } guard relies on no empty-block diagnostic; pre-decided disposition is file-the-output-and-halt, never post-clearance text touch; the same file-the-output-and-halt disposition is pre-decided for IntegerToString(probe_seq) (uint-to-long implicit conversion) and for the nine temps declared in the common region but populated only in the success arm). Emission cap: reserved sequences 1..20000 per C-reaching evaluation pass; a 20001st reaching evaluation emits the single STOPRESOLVE_CAP line (complete STOPRESOLVE CAP line per the P034 template, non-sequenced), sets probe_capped AND probe_dead first, and falls through with the run completing (hitting the cap is an acceptance miss; CAP is unreachable by bar count in a single uninterrupted tester execution in this envelope (s_lastBarTime and probe statics reset together on reinitialization; any reinitialization or multiple execution segment is recorded and fails the one-run equivalence unless expressly permitted) — cap-headroom bound: at most one C-reach per closed bar (3168 bars measured on the archive run, FRESHVETO-V1 G1), so the 20000 reservation cannot exhaust in one uninterrupted execution - retained strictly defensive. Expected count, mechanical: archive SIDE1E_STOPSHADOW rows = 13 and archive same-bar site-S5 SLEXT481 rows = 13 (zero set-diff both ways in FRESHVETO-V1); THE mandatory STAGE-0 enumeration, each labeled fire/non-fire/vetoed/generality (the seed label retires with the 16:55 demotion): 2026.08.26 14:40 generality (non-fire, veto-refused re-latch), 2026.08.27 17:00 non-fire, 2026.08.27 18:50 non-fire, 2026.08.28 10:00 fire, 2026.08.28 16:20 fire (A1 declined), 2026.08.31 15:05 non-fire, 2026.09.04 09:25 non-fire, 2026.09.04 10:35 vetoed (A2, SIDE1E without TP_ELECT), 2026.09.04 15:55 fire, 2026.09.07 