## 4. Acceptance (grade lines; actual path and shadow never interchanged; this probe output settles selector→slRef→gate→shadow ONLY — runtime ordering of veto/latch/SIGNAL/session-mark is settled by the filed source mapping plus diagnostic contract, never by probe-output proximity; offline state machine primary, counts as cross-checks; MANDATORY findings vs STRIKABLE scope)

Actual-path baseline: 7 TP_ELECT fire rows of 11 TP_ELECT rows total, where fire means a TP_ELECT row with R>=1.0 (archived 2-dp R by deliberate exception to the display-precision rule - all four non-fire rows sit outside the exact grading boundary) (archive: the 7 table bars, agreeing with the livePass=1 join; TP_ELECT rows carry no livePass field; A2 is livePass=1 with no TP_ELECT row, veto pre-latch, never a fire row; 4 further TP_ELECT rows print with R<1.0 (08-27 17:00 R0.35; 08-27 18:50 R0.18; 08-31 15:05 R0.34; 09-04 09:25 R0.63) and are non-fire baseline outside the 7-count) (A1 and A3 fire-but-declined among them; the print-only run itself keeps all 7 fire rows — the predicted post-activation count 6 from section 2 is the counterfactual (conditioned on N-2 producer-equality AND on absence of liveSel=-1 among the four sub-1.0 non-fire bars, discharged on archive per the B-5 pull with all four sel=1; channel (i) is not an N-2 consequence (hardest-load point: s1slot=-1-with-defined-ext1 rows widen only if producer rung 0 equals selector s0 - inside channel (ii) as written)), not this run's baseline); SIGNAL event counts reported separately under the comparison contract below. Under the print-only ext1 shadow, A3's record is leg-(a) consistent with wouldGate self-consistent (prediction under leg (b): printed rExt1 rounds to 0.68 with wouldGate=0 computed from printed operands); A1 likewise (prediction 1.38, pass) — both leg-(b) values archive-confirmed at display precision; new-run checks remain mandatory on archive rows. Table Rs grade by exact rational interval (no printed bands, no rounding): for numerator n tp-points and denominator d shadow-sl-points with d>1 at plus-or-minus 1 pt per distance, the interval is [(n-1)/(d+1), (n+1)/(d-1)]; the parsed binary64 rExt1 must lie inside, endpoints inclusive; the finite binary64 result is decoded to its exact integer ratio and compared by integer cross-products against those bounds, endpoints inclusive, and endpoints are never rounded to binary64 first; one common decoding rule governs every finite binary64 field: correctly rounded decimal-to-IEEE-754 binary64 conversion, round-to-nearest/ties-to-even, signed zero preserved; invalid or out-of-range decoded values fail before arithmetic; wouldGate Booleans stay exact recompute. Filed operands (tp-pts/sl-pts from archived five-decimal operands): 10:00 144/42; A1 108/78; 15:55 297/171; 09:15 180/37; 16:40 54/23; 10:05 133/53; A3 99/146. Actual-path rows grade the same exact-rational way from each row actual entry/sl/tp operands (display-precision artifacts 09-07 16:40 archived 2.34 vs 2.35-from-displays and 09-08 10:05 archived 2.52 vs 2.51-from-displays are interior to exact intervals, never misses) (leg-(a) self-consistency and wouldGate Booleans stay exact) — leg-(b) mismatch explained by printed currentPrice vs archived entry is report-only (finding with operands), never clearance failure; explanations are findings, never permission to accept a failed mandatory comparison (self-consistency plus the required A1 AND A3 self-consistent Booleans plus both records-at-C take precedence over the general tolerance); A2 is exempt from shadow-R/table acceptance only (mandatory ext1 acceptance is pxExt1/slot/provenance; A2 remains subject to the universal actualGate/live-operand checks, serialization checks, and terminal/diagnostic contract) (mandatory ext1: pxExt1 at archive precision + slot 13 + stamp/provenance; universal actualGate/live-operand/serialization/terminal/contract checks still apply); A2 signal-silence means no actual-path signal/fire outcome, while its probe line is expected. Offline validity is classified in four classes with Booleans preserved literally: live-input validity, live-quotient validity, shadow-input/quotient validity, diagnostic availability. The offline state machine is the primary structural validator with these transitions: first successful evaluation emits SCHEMA then NORMAL emitSeq=1; later successful evaluations emit exactly the next NORMAL sequence; BSAVE_FAIL carries exactly the next reserved sequence then permanent probe silence (post-terminal no-emission and post-terminal C-reach cardinality are source-structural only; output verifies only that no later STOPRESOLVE-family records appeared); CAP occurs only as the first C-reach after NORMAL 20000 then permanent probe silence (post-terminal no-emission and post-terminal C-reach cardinality are source-structural only; output verifies only that no later STOPRESOLVE-family records appeared); a first-evaluation BSAVE_FAIL carries no SCHEMA; duplicate, late, or post-terminal SCHEMA is invalid — count identities checked as independent cross-checks. Run prints gateConst (must equal numeric 1.0 and byte-equal StringFormat("%.17g", InpMinRewardRisk), RHS as consumed at L9670; the exact token is filed from the pre-build micro-check at STAGE-1 with anticipated token `1` under %g semantics for the frozen 1.0 input - a grader expecting `1.0` halts nothing, the filed token governs) and actualGate per evaluation — validated by per-record self-consistency (printed actualGate must equal the recompute from that record's printed currentPrice/slLive/tpPx/gateConst with binary64 reconstruction preserving the EA's subtraction, absolute-value, division, and comparison order under the language/compiler's documented double semantics — a one-ULP boundary ambiguity at exactly gateConst halts with operands, never an ordinary mismatch; any non-finite mandatory live operand is an independent acceptance failure terminating grading — never undecided; a non-finite EVALUATED live quotient is likewise an independent failure with literal actualGate preserved — finite guard-blocking with rLive='-' stays valid; "INVALID operand" always means the inputs relevant to that calculation; mismatch halts) plus the P034(c) operand-mapping identities as mandatory checks per record class (defined-finite reconstruct-and-compare; undefined-fallback pair/gate