 failure (ordering claims drop accordingly — the retained outcome requirements never drop); unobservable ordering on RETAINED obligations is unproved-and-halt (this halt applies to retained obligations only, never to expressly struck questions). A reduced-scope run never claims a struck question. Ordering/site report per the frozen mapping: stage order stop resolution, then R-gate, then veto, then latch, then SIGNAL, then session mark — asserted from control-flow reading plus the diagnostic contract, with runtime diagnostic evidence labeled separately from control-flow evidence; log proximity is not proof; pre-gate state never proves execution. 16:55 seed line — DEMOTED to FINDING (draft proposes, council disposes): no SESSION_LIMIT row at 16:55 exists on any date and no site=S5 row at 16:55 exists on any date, so no decline can be proved from the archive; the four evaluated-bar 16:55 SLEXT481 rows (2026.08.26 S2POLL, 2026.08.28 S3ARM, 2026.09.01 S2POLL, 2026.09.04 S2POLL) ride as S5-diagnostic context only. 17:00: dated 2026.08.27 17:00 post-gate presence proven in-archive (SIDE1E sel=1 + SIDE1X rows); presence/absence of any other dated 17:00 S5 evaluation comes from existing S5 diagnostics (ordered-occurrence matching: same key order on both sides, duplicates matched in order, never collapsed — S5 discoveries beyond 16:55/17:00/A2 are report-only under this rule); a newly visible S5 evaluation (17:00 or otherwise) is discovery evidence with operands — continuation depends on the contractual diagnostic comparison, never automatic. Halt for the actual-path contractual-diagnostic-equivalence check IFF the compared diagnostic set diverges from archive 8B2ED676 under the comparison contract (this iff governs the diagnostic-comparison component only; other mandatory failures halt independently) — row-for-row in run order over (barTime, site, event-kind) with ordered-occurrence duplicate matching: SIGNAL rows match on (barTime, dir) with the native mapping 1=LONG / -1=SHORT and halt on 0 (archive DirName text vs probe (int)g_dir); TP_ELECT rows match ONLY through the ordered-join path (archive TP_ELECT rows carry no dir field, so the direct key is never available for TP_ELECT); directionless TP_ELECT rows attribute dir ONLY through an unambiguous ordered join to the same-bar S5/SIDE record (multiplicity preserved, ambiguity halts; no inference from price relationships) (A3, N-15) and compare all price operands at archive precision (probe values formatted through the legacy five-decimal DoubleToString, then exact token equality; binary64 lossless prints are provenance transport, never the comparison basis) plus R within the exact-rational interval recomputed per row from actual operands after a validity check (NaN never passes); VETOCLEAR/SESSION_LIMIT rows match on (barTime, dir) and compare state/class exactly; S5 seed/presence rows (A2, dated 17:00s) match on (barTime, dir) and compare presence plus kind; the baseline source is archive 8B2ED676 named here so the comparator cannot drift; excluded metadata is exactly run/probe/wall-clock/terminal-build tags; duplicates matched in order with multiplicity preserved; sequence order preserved (membership alone never proves execution order); differences outside the contract's row set and field list are out of scope (never divergence, never satisfaction). Other mandatory checks (A2 record, slot equality per the fixed terms — MANDATORY: A2 slot==13; MANDATORY-WHEN-USED: namespace proof; FINDING: per-row ext1-vs-s0/s1 — degenerate gates, cap, unambiguous joins, prefix/tag presence, terminal exactly-once, count invariants, same-bar SIDE1E/SIDE1X external falsifier equalities) fail independently of this comparison. Offline count invariants, frozen here: SIDE1E_STOPSHADOW count must equal NORMAL plus BSAVE_FAIL plus CAP plus subsequent probe-silent C-reaches (exact equality when no terminal record exists; archive prediction 13; depends on InpDebugLog=true since SIDE1E prints inside the L9683